---
<Layout title="Research | Zhiqian Chen">
  <main class="container">
    <nav class="top-nav" aria-label="Sections">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <a href="/research" aria-current="page">Research</a>
      <a href="/grant">Grant</a>
      <a href="/people">People</a>
      <a href="/teach">Teach</a>
      <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=NC3-O6UAAAAJ&hl=en&oi=ao" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Paper <i class="ai ai-google-scholar-square ai-sm nav-ghost"></i> <i class="fas fa-arrow-up-right-from-square nav-ghost"></i></a>
      <a href="https://substack.com/@zhiqianchen1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Zhiqian's Note <svg class="nav-ghost nav-substack" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" width="11" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22.539 8.242H1.46V5.406h21.08v2.836zM1.46 10.812V24L12 18.11 22.54 24V10.812H1.46zM22.54 0H1.46v2.836h21.08V0z"/></svg> <i class="fas fa-arrow-up-right-from-square nav-ghost"></i></a>
    </nav>

    <section class="hero">
      <h1>Research Statement</h1>
      <p class="lead">COVID-19 has caused over 6 million deaths worldwide since late 2019 and an estimated $12.5 trillion in economic loss as of 2024. The pandemic exposed deep vulnerabilities in modern networked systems — disrupted supply chains, financial market volatility, misinformation amplified across social networks. The July 2024 CrowdStrike update failure brought airlines, hospitals, and businesses to a standstill worldwide, underscoring how far cascading effects travel inside interconnected systems. Climate change, pandemics, and food security all run on interdependent networks — transportation, finance, supply chains, ecology, social networks — that form the backbone of our societal and economic infrastructure. As the world grows more interconnected, resilient and interpretable network models become essential.</p>
      <blockquote class="statement">
        <strong>Research interest.</strong> I explore the fundamental principles of networked system dynamics by integrating machine learning, network science, and dynamical systems theory. The work spans theoretical innovation and practical application, and centers on efficient, interpretable models that improve decision-making in real-world contexts.
      </blockquote>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Current research</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">I study graph dynamics through spectral graph theory, uncertainty quantification, higher-order analysis, and physics-inspired methods. My current focus is the behavior of coupled and interdependent networks — prevalent in practice, but still thinly developed.</p>
      <div class="cards two">
        {pillars.map((p) => (
          <article class="card">
            <h3>{p.label}</h3>
            <ul class="topics">
              {p.topics.map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p><strong>Theoretical study.</strong> Developing new methodology to represent and analyze graphs and their dynamics. I have explored spectral graph theory as a unified framework for representing complex networks — several papers, a survey, tutorials at prestigious venues, and a widely used paper collection. I also investigate higher-order methods such as Shapley values and Sobol indices to understand combinatorial interactions among nodes, and use Bayesian optimization, Gaussian processes, and Kalman filtering to address efficiency in graph-based problems.</p>
        <p><strong>Application research.</strong> The work reaches key social infrastructure and biological networks: transportation and urban systems, spatial epidemiology, and genetic networks. Collaborations with ecologists, medical researchers, and engineers have extended these methods to ecological networks, circuit dynamics, and brain signals in conditions such as ADHD and sleep disorders.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Funded projects</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">External support totals <strong>$11,196,037</strong>, with <strong>$1,665,222</strong> in personal funding credits.</p>
      <ol class="projects">
        {projects.map((p) => (
          <li class="project">
            <div class="project-head">
              <span class="project-funder">{p.funder}</span>
              <span class="project-role">{p.role}</span>
              <span class="project-amount">{p.amount}</span>
              {p.period && <span class="project-period">{p.period}</span>}
              {p.award && (p.href
                ? <a class="project-award" href={p.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{p.award} <i class="fas fa-arrow-up-right-from-square" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
                : <span class="project-award">{p.award}</span>)}
            </div>
            <p class="project-title">{p.title}</p>
            <p class="project-desc">{p.desc}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Collaborators</h2>
      <p class="prose-p">To reach both theoretical insight and applicable outcomes — and to keep a full perspective on the problem — I work with faculty and researchers across mathematics, social science, cybersecurity, power and circuit networks, epidemiology, veterinary medicine, animal science, healthcare, and psychology. These collaborations, at both the paper and grant level, span USDA, UC Davis, George Mason University, the University of Connecticut, Emory University, the University of Mississippi Medical Center, and the University of Georgia, among others.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Future plan</h2>
      <div class="cards three">
        {futurePlan.map((f, i) => (
          <article class="card">
            <span class="card-mark">{i + 1}</span>
            <h3>{f.title}</h3>
            <p>{f.desc}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p><strong>Funding.</strong> I intend to keep applying this research to significant application domains — power grids, disease transmission, supply chain management, financial systems — and to build support through federal programs that align with graph dynamics, cross-network behavior, and data-driven modeling: NSF MPS for fluid dynamics and spectral methods, NSF CCF for algorithmic foundations and robust intelligence, and NSF III for real applications. NSF ENG programs in materials research and biological systems fit where a project connects to graph representations of physical or biological processes. Work on disease transmission, intervention planning, and biomedical networks motivates NIH applications; coupled infrastructure, energy systems, and uncertainty in large interconnected networks guide DOE applications. I also seek industry partnerships for translational studies on complex systems.</p>
        <p><strong>Reach-out.</strong> I plan to expand connections with experts in material science, circuit modeling, quantum computing, financial mathematics, power grids, biomedical and biological systems, disease transmission, transportation systems, dynamical systems, and network science.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="deadlines">
      <h2>Deadlines · Sep 2026 – Feb 2027</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">Funding, papers, and service — {deadlineCount} dated items. Verify each against its own solicitation; a date falling on a weekend or federal holiday shifts to the next business day, and NIH resubmissions run one month later (Mar / Jul / Nov).</p>
      <ul class="legend">
        {Object.entries(kindLabels).map(([k, label]) => (
          <li><span class={`dot dot-${k}`} aria-hidden="true"></span>{label}</li>
        ))}
        <li><span class="dot dot-est" aria-hidden="true"></span>Estimated date</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="months">
        {deadlines.map((m) => (
          <section class="month">
            <h3>{m.month}</h3>
            <ul class="deadline-list">
              {m.items.map((d) => (
                <li class={`deadline kind-${d.kind}${d.est ? ' is-est' : ''}`}>
                  <span class="deadline-date">{d.date}<span class="deadline-day">{d.day}</span></span>
                  <span class="deadline-name">{d.name}{d.est && <span class="est-flag">est.</span>}</span>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </section>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="cards three open-calls">
        {openCalls.map((c) => (
          <article class="card">
            <h3>{c.heading}</h3>
            <ul class="topics">
              {c.items.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
<style>
  :root { --accent:#2563eb; --ink:#0f172a; --muted:#475569; }
  .container { max-width: min(95vw, 1600px); margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; box-sizing: border-box; }
  .top-nav { margin-bottom: 14px; padding: 10px 0 14px; display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:8px; align-items:center; background:transparent; border:none; border-bottom:none; border-radius:0; box-shadow:none; }
  .top-nav a { text-decoration:none; color:var(--ink); font-family:'Montserrat',sans-serif; font-size:.9rem; padding:7px 10px; border-radius:999px; background:transparent; }
  .top-nav a:hover { background: #f1f5f9; color: #0f172a; }
  .top-nav a[aria-current="page"] { background: #e2e8f0; color: #0f172a; box-shadow: inset 0 1px 2px rgba(15,23,42,0.10); }
  .nav-ghost { font-size:.78rem; margin-left:4px; opacity:.85; }
  .nav-substack { vertical-align: -1px; opacity: .85; }

  .hero { margin: 10px 0 28px; }
  .hero h1 { font-family:'Montserrat',sans-serif; font-size:2rem; margin:0 0 10px; }
  .lead { margin:0; color:var(--muted); max-width:80ch; font-size:.95rem; line-height:1.6; }
  .statement { margin:16px 0 0; max-width:80ch; padding:14px 16px; border-left:3px solid var(--accent); border-radius:0 12px 12px 0; background:#f8fafc; color:#1e293b; font-size:1rem; line-height:1.6; }
  .statement strong { color:var(--ink); }

  .section { padding-top:18px; margin-top:26px; border-top:1px solid rgba(148,163,184,.18); }
  .section h2 { font-family:'Montserrat',sans-serif; font-size:1.1rem; margin:0 0 12px; }
  .section-lead { margin:0 0 14px; color:var(--muted); max-width:80ch; font-size:.92rem; line-height:1.55; }
  .prose { margin-top:14px; }
  .prose p, .prose-p { margin:0 0 10px; color:#334155; max-width:80ch; font-size:.93rem; line-height:1.6; }
  .prose p:last-child { margin-bottom:0; }

  .cards { display:grid; gap:14px; }
